        "translation": "### 1.3 滑移反射 (Glide reflections)\n\n更重要的是，箭头对这些女孩来说比单纯的向量或平移具有更广泛的含义。她们两年前就开始学习关系了。她们经常用箭头——曲线箭头——在“土豆”（她们对集合元素的通俗称呼）之间表示关系。她们在这里所做的只是以前所做工作的特殊情况。她们将转换视为特殊的关系。她们学习几何的背景比通常的孩子要广泛得多。这里不仅整合了“综合”和“解析”几何；整个几何学被合并成了一个以集合和关系为基础的统一数学课程。这些曲线箭头清楚地指出了这一点。\n\n> Still more important, arrows have a much wider meaning for these girls than just vectors or translations. They began the study of relations two years earlier. They often represented relations by arrows - curved arrows - between points of ‘potatoes’, which meant for them elements of sets. What they are doing here is just a particular case of what they did formerly. They consider transformations as special relations. They learn geometry in a much broader context than children usually do. Not only ‘synthetic’ and ‘analytic’ geometry are here integrated; the whole of geometry is merged into a unified mathematics course, based on sets and relations. These curved arrows point it out clearly."
