        "translation": "### 1.8 (续) - 代码引入\n\n矩阵的引入可以通过代码完成。例如：\nA B C D E F G H I ... 用数字表示。\nBUDA 可以通过编写相应的数字并左乘一个“编码器”矩阵（例如 $\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}$）来加密。矩阵相乘的规则直接给出，不作解释。一行“跳水”到一列（row 'diving' onto a column）的概念被发现非常有用。\n\n> Introduction to matrices can be made via codes. For example: A B C D E F G H I ... are represented by numbers. BUDA can be encoded by writing down the corresponding numbers and premultiplying by an ‘encoder’ matrix (e.g. $\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}$). The rule for multiplying matrices is stated without explanation. The notion of a row ‘diving’ onto a column has been found useful.\n\n消息以加密形式发送。在另一端，解密通过乘以“解码器”矩阵来实现。在这之后，有足够的空间来进行发现：例如，学生可以发现：(a) 为给定编码器寻找正确解码器的规则，(b) 单位矩阵和零矩阵，(c) 他们正在进行模 26 的算术运算，(d) 编码器的行列式应为 1 以避免出现分数。\n\n> The message is then sent in encoded form. At the other end, decoding is effected through multiplication by a ‘decoder’ matrix. After this artificial start, there is plenty of scope for discoveries: for example, pupils can discover: (a) the rule for finding the correct decoder for a given encoder, (b) the unit and zero matrices, (c) that they are working modulo 26, (d) that the determinant of the encoder should be 1 to avoid fractions."
