        "page": 77,
        "translation": "### 1.8 (续) - 符号的陷阱\n\n滥用符号 $\\therefore$ (“因此”) 的危害可以通过以下演示呈现：\n$x+2y = 5$\n$3x+6y = 11$\n$\\therefore \\begin{bmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{bmatrix} = \\dots \\implies 0 = 8$\n这阵可怕的点状雪崩产生了一个荒谬的结论。如果将 $\\therefore$ 替换为蕴含符号 $\\Rightarrow$（且除非每一步都显然可逆，否则不使用 $\\Leftrightarrow$），那么最后的例子就读起来非常合乎逻辑。正如英国谚语所说：“问个傻问题，你会得到个傻答案。”\n\n> The pernicious use of the symbol $\\therefore$ (‘therefore’) can be brought out by the following demonstration: $x+2y = 5$, $3x+6y = 11$, $\\therefore \\begin{bmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{bmatrix} = \\dots \\implies 0 = 8$. This horrible snowstorm of dots has produced an absurdity. If ‘therefore’ is replaced by the implication sign $\\Rightarrow$ (and unless every step is clearly reversible, $\\Leftrightarrow$ is not used), then the last example reads quite logically. As the English proverb says: ‘Ask a silly question and you get a silly answer.’"
