        "translation": "### 2.6 电影与动画 (Films and Animation)\n\n电影作为教具具有独特的优势：它能展示**运动中的图形**。静态的教科书插图往往无法传达某些动态过程，如旋转、缩放或轨迹的形成。\n\n> Films as teaching aids have unique advantages: they show figures in movement. Static textbook illustrations often fail to convey dynamic processes like rotation or scaling.\n\n我们将重点讨论 Nicolet 的微电影。这些影片通常只有几分钟长，没有对白，纯粹通过视觉逻辑呈现数学思想。这种方式迫使学生通过观察进行思考，而不是被动地听取解释。\n\n> We will focus on Nicolet’s micro-films. These films are typically a few minutes long, have no soundtrack, and present mathematical ideas purely through visual logic."
